    "normalization": "Only the actual PID in the two native status prefixes and observation.pid is replaced with0 for fixed whole-trace byte/hash comparison; every other byte, sorted field order, LF and byte-array element stays unchanged.",
    "writer_work": "Loose deterministic write-call ceilings discriminate buffered complete records from one write per JSON byte.9000covers both8MiB0xff streams expanded to~64MiB; partial-write case has its own larger ceiling relative to output size. This does not increase any runtime resource/deadline ceiling.",
    "error_policy": "An IO failure discards pending observation-buffer bytes without Drop replay; explicit required cleanup/error traces may follow. Preserve underlying IO kind. A failed serialization does not trigger a second flush. Final successful flush remains inside operation deadline.",
    "native_receipts": "A real owned test-peer process emits both prepared byte files in a dedicated trace-streams mode. A separate explicit test context records its actual launch/status; no exit completion is recorded during bounded preparation wait. observe must create the explicit completion on success and all errors. Ambient context, where present, is completed separately after checking explicit receipt and remains unchanged.",
    "preparation_failures": "Three real owned filesystem failures before observe. Launch denial is proved by failed create_new before spawn; already-selected /bin/sleep10 must still be running before B recording and is actually killed/reaped. No fabricated B receipt is allowed. Other test-peer children really exit0 before missing-exits/read_dir and trace-path/create_new faults. Rename only the owned empty B exits directory to preserve it. Independent local fallback A records every real child/status even when B cannot; ambient source context, where active, completes separately without mutation. Restore only owned launch permissions promptly; unsupported/root write denial is failure, never skip/PASS. The original preparation error and all cleanup/completion outcomes are retained. Successful old14 preparation still leaves B completion solely to observe."
  },
